Package: bdscrub
Title: Clean Bangladesh-Specific Data Fields
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    c(person("Ishtiaq Mahmud", "Fahim", , "imfahim28@isrt.ac.bd", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Humaira", "Kashmi", role = "aut"))
Description: Cleans the fields that make Bangladeshi survey and
    administrative data messy. Reads mobile numbers in any format (also
    several per cell), money amounts written with lakh, crore, Bangla
    (Bengali) digits or as ranges, and plain numbers. Maps the many
    spellings of district, division and thana (upazila) names, in English
    or Bangla, to standard names, codes and the spellings used in
    administrative boundary files, and reads the post code, thana, district
    and division from free-text addresses using the Bangladesh Post office
    list. Every correction is reported. Includes functions to check and
    clean whole data frames. Works offline and depends on base R only.
